  {
    "title": "Wellness gives the challenge a human purpose",
    "seconds": 60,
    "notes": "Our first proposed wellness challenge is a better welcome at a wellness centre. Imagine a visitor who needs to find an activity room. The robot explains the options: guide me, call a staff member, or cancel. The visitor stays in control. Teams can compete to make this interaction clearer and more useful. We would evaluate task completion, whether people understand the next step, and whether cancellation or staff handoff works. We also want participants to tell us how comfortable they feel. Our current HRI demo records interaction events and outcomes in simulation. It does not prove a health benefit. The next step is testing with real users and a partner venue.",
